ECL 26.5.5 library transition
===========================

The proposed package set is:

  ecl         26.5.5+dfsg-1
  maxima-sage 5.50.0-3
  sagemath    10.9-4

Debian's maxima-sage and python3-sage binaries link to libecl. Both must
be rebuilt for libecl26.5. The old and new runtime libraries can coexist,
but the shared /usr/lib/ecl/maxima.fas pathname must contain a module
matching the ECL library used by its loader. Loading the newly compiled
Maxima module with the old Sage ECL extension was reproduced as a memory
access error followed by a segmentation fault.

To prevent a partial upgrade from mixing these modules:

  * ecl Breaks maxima-sage versions before 5.50.0-3~.
  * maxima-sage requires ecl >= 26.5.5+dfsg-1~ and Breaks python3-sage
    versions before 10.9-4~.
  * sagemath requires the updated ECL and maxima-sage packages at build
    time and runtime; its ECL development dependency is also versioned.

Coordinate these source versions when preparing the transition. If a
maintainer chooses different Debian revisions, update the corresponding
versioned relationships in all three source packages together. The
changelogs remain UNRELEASED pending maintainer adoption and upload.

Review branches:

https://github.com/dimpase/ecl-debian/tree/update/ecl-26.5.5
https://github.com/dimpase/maxima-sage-debian/tree/update/ecl-26.5.5
https://github.com/dimpase/sagemath-debian/tree/update/ecl-26.5.5

The archive source dependency check also found SBCL using ECL as its
bootstrap compiler on sh4 only. Its binaries do not need a libecl ABI
transition. The Common Lisp source packages that test ECL, and packages
accepting the virtual lisp-compiler dependency, do not ship modules
linked to libecl that need an archive rebuild.

Validation was performed in Debian unstable arm64, restricted to four
CPUs. Maxima's complete binary package was built; Sage's ECL extension
was rebuilt in the installed Sage 10.9 package, and all 204 ECL doctests
and focused embedded-Maxima checks passed. A full Sage package rebuild
and the sh4 SBCL bootstrap have not been performed here.
